Use `ConfigureLifecycleEvents` in `MauiProgram.cs`:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity =>
        {
            // Runs when activity loses focus
        })
        .OnStop(activity =>
        {
            // Runs when activity is no longer visible
        }));
#elif IOS || MACCATALYST
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app =>
        {
            // Runs when app enters background
        }));
#endif
});
```

**Cross-platform alternative:** If you don't need the native callback specifically, override `OnStopped` on a `Window` subclass — it maps to `OnStop` on Android and `DidEnterBackground` on iOS automatically:

```csharp
public class AppWindow : Window
{
    public AppWindow(Page page) : base(page) { }

    protected override void OnStopped()
    {
        base.OnStopped();
        // Save state here — fires on both platforms
    }
}
```

Return it from `App.CreateWindow`:

```csharp
protected override Window CreateWindow(IActivationState? activationState)
    => new AppWindow(new AppShell());
```

**Key tips:**
- `OnPause` (Android) maps to the cross-platform `Deactivated` event (app may still be visible).
- `OnStop` / `DidEnterBackground` maps to the cross-platform `Stopped` event.
- Keep handlers fast (<2s) to avoid ANR on Android or watchdog kills on iOS.
